{
  "name": "Generate missing excerpts for WordPress posts with OpenAI",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "d0000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Template Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -40,
        -760
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 860,
        "content": "# Generate missing excerpts for WordPress posts with OpenAI\n\n## Who's it for\nWordPress site owners, content marketers and SEO teams with many posts that have no hand-written excerpt.\n\n## How it works\nEvery week, or on demand, the workflow fetches your latest posts and keeps published ones that have no excerpt and enough content. OpenAI then writes a short plain-text excerpt in the same language as the post. Dry run mode is on by default and only shows the generated excerpts, so nothing changes on your site. When you turn it off, each excerpt is saved back to WordPress through the REST API. Invalid AI output is skipped.\n\n## How to set up\n1. In WordPress, open Users, Profile, Application Passwords and create a new password.\n2. Add your WordPress API and OpenAI credentials in n8n.\n3. Open the **Workflow Configuration** node and set your site URL, posts to scan, posts per run, model and excerpt length.\n4. Click Execute workflow with dryRun set to true and review the excerpts.\n5. Set dryRun to false and activate the workflow.\n\n## Requirements\n- WordPress 5.6 or higher with the REST API and Application Passwords enabled\n- OpenAI API key\n- n8n Cloud or self-hosted n8n\n\n## How to customize the workflow\n- Edit the prompt to match your brand voice.\n- Change the schedule or the number of posts per run.\n- Add a Slack or email step to report which posts were updated."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -40,
        140
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 560,
        "content": "### 1. Start and configure\nRun it manually or weekly. Edit your settings in **Workflow Configuration**. Keep `dryRun` set to true until you are happy with the results."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        400,
        140
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 700,
        "height": 560,
        "content": "### 2. Find posts that need an excerpt\nFetches posts in edit context so the raw excerpt is visible. Keeps published posts with no excerpt and at least 200 characters of content, then caps the batch to control cost."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1120,
        140
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 900,
        "height": 560,
        "content": "### 3. Write the excerpt with AI\nHTML is stripped from the post, OpenAI returns a short excerpt as JSON, and the result is validated. Bad or empty output is skipped instead of saved."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2040,
        140
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 560,
        "content": "### 4. Preview or update\nWith dry run on, excerpts are only shown in the node output. With dry run off, each excerpt is saved to WordPress using the REST API and your WordPress credential."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Run Manually",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "position": [
        0,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {},
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Run Weekly",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
        0,
        260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "weeks",
              "triggerAtDay": [
                1
              ],
              "triggerAtHour": 9
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Workflow Configuration",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        240,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "siteUrl",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "https://your-site.example.com"
            },
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "postsToScan",
              "type": "number",
              "value": 100
            },
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "maxPostsPerRun",
              "type": "number",
              "value": 10
            },
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "openAiModel",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "gpt-4o-mini"
            },
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "excerptMaxWords",
              "type": "number",
              "value": 30
            },
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "dryRun",
              "type": "boolean",
              "value": true
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Get Posts from WordPress",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.wordpress",
      "position": [
        480,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "limit": "={{ $('Workflow Configuration').first().json.postsToScan }}",
        "resource": "post",
        "operation": "getAll",
        "returnAll": false,
        "additionalFields": {
          "context": "edit"
        }
      },
      "credentials": {
        "wordpressApi": {
          "id": "credential-id",
          "name": "WordPress account"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "Keep Posts Without Excerpt",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.filter",
      "position": [
        720,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "e+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.status }}",
              "rightValue": "publish"
            },
            {
              "id": "e+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "empty",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ ($json.excerpt?.raw ?? '').trim() }}",
              "rightValue": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "e+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "gte"
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ ($json.content?.raw ?? '').length }}",
              "rightValue": 200
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000006",
      "name": "Limit Posts Per Run",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.limit",
      "position": [
        960,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "maxItems": "={{ $('Workflow Configuration').first().json.maxPostsPerRun }}"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000007",
      "name": "Prepare Post Text",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        1200,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "postId",
              "type": "number",
              "value": "={{ $json.id }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "title",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.title?.raw ?? $json.title?.rendered ?? '' }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "plainText",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ ($json.content?.raw ?? '').replace(/<[^>]+>/g, ' ').replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim().slice(0, 4000) }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000008",
      "name": "Write Excerpt with OpenAI",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "position": [
        1440,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 30000
        },
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ model: $('Workflow Configuration').first().json.openAiModel, response_format: { type: 'json_object' }, messages: [{ role: 'system', content: 'You write concise WordPress post excerpts. Return only JSON in this shape: {\"excerpt\": \"text\"}. Write plain text in the same language as the post, with no HTML and no quotation marks. Use at most ' + $('Workflow Configuration').first().json.excerptMaxWords + ' words. Summarize the main point and make readers want to continue. Do not invent facts.' }, { role: 'user', content: 'Title: ' + $json.title + '\\n\\nContent: ' + $json.plainText } ] }) }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType",
        "nodeCredentialType": "openAiApi"
      },
      "credentials": {
        "openAiApi": {
          "id": "credential-id",
          "name": "OpenAI account"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000009",
      "name": "Validate AI Excerpt",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        1680,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "\nconst post = $('Prepare Post Text').item.json;\nlet excerpt = '';\nlet aiFailed = true;\n\ntry {\n  const content = $input.item.json.choices[0].message.content;\n  excerpt = String(JSON.parse(content).excerpt || '').replace(/<[^>]+>/g, '').trim();\n  aiFailed = excerpt.length < 20 || excerpt.length > 400;\n} catch (e) {\n  // Leave aiFailed as true so this post is skipped\n}\n\nreturn { json: { postId: post.postId, title: post.title, excerpt, aiFailed } };\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000010",
      "name": "Is Excerpt Valid?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        1920,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "e+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "false",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.aiFailed }}",
              "rightValue": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "d0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000011",
      "name": "Is Dry Run Enabled?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        2160,
        300
